Summary
In the scripted/AUTO setup path, environment variables are normalized into property keys by normalizeEnvVariableKey, but the normalization cannot produce several of the underscore-separated keys the wizard actually reads. Those env vars are silently dropped and the corresponding fields fall back to their defaults — most importantly createDatabasePassword (default empty) and createDatabaseUsername (default root), producing Access denied for user 'root'@... (using password: NO).
The two pieces
Env vars are run through normalizeEnvVariableKey before being stored as properties (InitializationFilter lines 339–342):
getEnvironmentVariables().forEach((key, value) -> {
    String normalizedKey = normalizeEnvVariableKey(key);
    script.setProperty(normalizedKey, value);
});
The normalizer (lines 1929–1934):
private String normalizeEnvVariableKey(String envVarKey) {
    if (NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS.contains(envVarKey)) {
        return envVarKey.toLowerCase();          // keep underscores
    }
    return envVarKey.toLowerCase().replace('_', '.');  // underscores -> dots
}
The allow-list (lines 198–200):
private static final Set<String> NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS = new HashSet<>(
    Arrays.asList("INSTALL_METHOD", "DATABASE_NAME", "HAS_CURRENT_OPENMRS_DATABASE", "CREATE_DATABASE_USER",
        "CREATE_TABLES", "ADD_DEMO_DATA", "MODULE_WEB_ADMIN", "AUTO_UPDATE_DATABASE", "ADMIN_USER_PASSWORD"));
The conflict
The property keys the wizard reads (lines 354–395) mix two naming conventions:
dot-separated: connection.url, connection.username, connection.password

underscore-separated: database_name, create_database_username, create_database_password, create_user_username, create_user_password, create_tables, create_database_user, …

The NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS allow-list is incomplete. Missing keys:
CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME

CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD

CREATE_USER_USERNAME

CREATE_USER_PASSWORD

CONNECTION_DRIVER_CLASS

All of these are incorrectly translated into . formats but only the underscore formats are read.

The registration configuration allows a user to configure where to navigate after a patient is saved. The default is the patient chart. 
As we have started adding O3 apps and features to the PIH Malawi EMR, we want to have the ability to navigate to an old patient dashboard, which is a non SPA page. This is where I discovered this bug that when I try the following configuration the system resolved the URL to undefined.
"@openmrs/esm-patient-registration-app": {
  "links": {
    "submitButton": "${openmrsBase}/patientDashboard.form?patientId=${patientUuid}"
  },
  }
